   <text>
      <body>
         <div type="letter">
                <div type="mainBody">
                    <p>Il mio numero di casa è 42</p> <p>
                        <add place="Text is integrated into image. See “Images” section on this page">
                            <foreign xml:lang="eng">to wish you</foreign>
                        </add> <foreign xml:lang="fra">Joyeux Noël</foreign>
                    </p>  <closer>
                        <dateline>
                            <name type="geo" key="G_FRA_PARI">Paris</name> ’33</dateline>
                        <signed>
                            <name type="person" key="joyc82">James Joyce</name>
                        </signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
                <div type="translation">
                    <p>My house number is 42</p> <p>
                        <add place="Text is integrated into image. See “Images” section on this page">to wish you</add> Merry Christmas</p> <closer>
                        <dateline>Paris ’33</dateline>
                        <signed>James Joyce</signed>
                    </closer>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div type="notes">
                <note xml:id="global-note1" type="global">This postcard shows a black-and-white view of l’Avenue de l’Opéra looking towards the Paris Opéra. The image was published in Paris by Éditions d’art “Yvon”, taken from a photograph by “Yvon,” born Pierre Yves-Petit (1886-1969), who launched a postcard business, Éditions d’art d’Yvon, from his family’s home in Neuilly-sur-Seine (Beatrice Thornton, “Yvon’s Paris,” at http://www.artnet.com/magazineus/reviews/thornton/yvons-paris-1-18-11.asp).</note>
            </div>
      </body>
